---
description: Never expose secrets - applies to every task in this repo
alwaysApply: true
---
- Never print, echo, log, display, or paste any secret: API keys, tokens, passwords, credentials, private keys, Authorization headers, cookies, or the VALUE of any environment variable.
- Never output the contents of .env*, ~/.git-credentials, the macOS keychain, `gh auth token`, `vercel env pull`, or any credential store.
- Never use flags or env vars that can print credentials: GIT_TRACE, GIT_CURL_VERBOSE, GIT_TRACE_PACKET, `curl -v` with auth headers, `set -x` around secrets, or any --verbose/--debug mode on git/gh/vercel/supabase commands that authenticate.
- To confirm a secret exists, check presence or length only (e.g. `test -n "$VAR" && echo set`), never the value.
- Never generate secrets inside the chat or the agent terminal. Tell Lior to generate them herself in her own terminal.
- If any output might contain a secret, redact it before showing it. If a secret was exposed anyway, STOP immediately and tell Lior exactly which secret and where it appeared, so she can revoke it.
- If a push/auth command fails, report the error message only - do not retry with verbose or debug output.
